---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import HowICanHelp from '../components/HowICanHelp.astro';
import { UTC_OFFSET } from '../timezone';

const utcSuffix = UTC_OFFSET > 0 ? `+${UTC_OFFSET}` : UTC_OFFSET < 0 ? `${UTC_OFFSET}` : '';
---

<Base>
  <div class="mb5 mh3 mh4-ns">
    <div class="mb5">
      <h1 class="mt5">Martin Klepsch</h1>
      <span>People × Technology</span>
    </div>
    <div class="mw6 lh-copy">
      <p>
        I'm a software consultant with a focus on user interfaces and development
        tooling. This interest got me into Clojure and ClojureScript and these two eventually
        became my favorite tools for most of my work.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lately I've been working remotely with various companies using Clojure/Script
        shipping features, taming codebases and improving their Clojure practices.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're looking for some help with your project, just <a class="lined" href="mailto:martinklepsch@googlemail.com">shoot me an email</a>. While I'm most
        experienced with Clojure different language choices can also be interesting.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm also interested in the challenges of building up product teams (especially
        distributed ones) and developing workflows that are both flexible for team members and
        efficient in time and quality.
      </p>
      <p>I'm currently in timezone UTC{utcSuffix}. <span id="utc-offset"></span></p>
      <p>
        You can also follow what I'm up to on <a class="lined" href="https://twitter.com/martinklepsch">Twitter</a> &amp; <a class="lined" href="https://github.com/martinklepsch">GitHub</a>.
      </p>

      <HowICanHelp />
    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    import '../scripts/utc-offset';
  </script>
</Base>
